sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CALLER as Any status-transition site<br/>(orders / payments / fulfillment)
    participant SEAM as orders.service.on_order_status_changed
    participant RT as realtime.publish_order_event
    participant W as merchants.webhooks.enqueue
    participant DB as Postgres (caller's transaction)
    participant WK as apps/worker (M3a Task 4)

    Note over CALLER: order.status and order.updated_at are already set

    CALLER->>SEAM: on_order_status_changed(db, order)

    alt publish_realtime (the default)
        SEAM->>RT: {type: order.status_changed, orderId, status, at}
        Note right of RT: no-op when order.user_id IS NULL --<br/>which every merchant order is.<br/>That is why the webhook needed a seam<br/>rather than riding this call.
    end

    alt order.merchant_id IS NULL -- retail
        SEAM-->>CALLER: None, nothing enqueued
    else a merchant order
        SEAM->>W: enqueue(merchant_id, order.status_changed, payload)
        W->>DB: SELECT merchant_webhooks WHERE merchant_id AND disabled_at IS NULL
        alt no hook, or disabled
            W-->>CALLER: None -- the outbox holds only deliverable work
        else configured and enabled
            W->>DB: flush the caller's pending writes (outside the savepoint)
            W->>DB: SAVEPOINT
            W->>DB: INSERT merchant_webhook_deliveries<br/>(status=pending, url=<snapshot>, payload)
            W->>DB: SELECT pg_notify('merchant_webhook_queue', delivery_id)
            alt IntegrityError / DataError -- our bug, never a merchant's input
                W->>DB: ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
                W->>W: log.error(type + SQLSTATE only, never the driver's<br/>message -- it renders the failing row, url included)
                W-->>CALLER: None -- the order still commits
                Note over W,DB: An order is money; a webhook is a courtesy.
            else inserted
                W-->>CALLER: delivery_id
            end
        end
    end

    CALLER->>DB: COMMIT (or ROLLBACK)
    alt COMMIT
        DB-->>WK: NOTIFY merchant_webhook_queue, delivery_id
        WK->>DB: claim FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, deliver (Task 4)
    else ROLLBACK
        Note over DB,WK: the row AND the NOTIFY are dropped together --<br/>a merchant is never told about a sale that did not happen
    end
